# Transient factory workspace data. Candidate/blueprint/review-queue state
# is generated and moved by the pipeline; it is not durable project history
# and must not be committed. Published manifests are the one durable audit
# trail and stay tracked — questions-assemble-bank reads them to build the
# shipped bank.
#
# reports/ used to be unignored here on the same "durable audit trail"
# reasoning, which put 4,252 gate reports into git. They are orchestrator
# output, reproducible from the pipeline, and nothing reads them: the tests
# build their own mkdtemp() workspaces through the
# MINDMOSAIC_QUESTION_FACTORY_ROOT override rather than touching this tree
# (src/tests/unit/question-factory/cli-test-helpers.ts). The `!reports/**`
# line is gone, so `*` now covers them and the four dated session-WIP paths
# that used to punch back through it are no longer needed.
*
!.gitignore
!*/
!.gitkeep
!published-manifests/**

# Hand-authored blueprint *templates* (curriculum seeds checked in as worked
# examples for a new subject foundation) are durable source, not pipeline
# output — unlike everything else under blueprints/, which is
# generated/moved by the pipeline and stays untracked. Scoped to a
# `-seed-*` suffix so pipeline-generated blueprints (no such suffix) remain
# ignored by default.
!blueprints/*-seed-*.json
